Employee Attrition Prediction System

By: Prathamesh Arvind Kodag
Date: September 2, 2025

Abstract

Employee attrition is a significant challenge for organizations, leading to increased recruitment costs and loss of productivity. This project builds a machine learning system to predict whether an employee is likely to leave a company, using the IBM HR Analytics Employee Attrition dataset. The system leverages Python, scikit-learn, and Streamlit to enable HR teams to proactively identify at-risk employees and design retention strategies.

1. Introduction

Employee turnover can severely impact organizational performance. Early identification of potential attrition helps HR teams take corrective actions. This project focuses on predicting employee attrition using historical HR data and provides insights into the key factors driving attrition.

Objectives:

Predict employee attrition using machine learning.

Understand the main factors influencing attrition.

Deploy an interactive tool for HR teams.

2. Dataset Description

Source: IBM HR Analytics Employee Attrition dataset

Rows: 1470

Features: 35 (26 numeric, 9 categorical)

Target Variable: Attrition (Yes/No → encoded as 1/0)

Key features: Age, Job Role, Marital Status, Overtime, Job Satisfaction, Work-Life Balance, Years at Company, etc.


