6. Key Insights

Younger employees with shorter tenure are more likely to leave.

Overtime is the strongest predictor of attrition (30% vs 10%).

JobRole impacts attrition: Sales Representatives (~40%) vs Research Directors (~2.5%).

Single employees are more likely to leave than married employees.

High job satisfaction and good work-life balance reduce attrition.

Placeholder for feature importance plot:

Figure 7: Feature importance from Logistic Regression

7. Conclusion & Future Work

This system enables HR teams to predict attrition and understand its driving factors. The project highlights the importance of work-life balance, overtime, and job role in employee retention.

Future Enhancements:

Batch predictions via uploaded CSV files.

Production deployment with FastAPI + Docker.

Use SMOTE or class weights to improve recall on the minority class.

